"CONTROLS\",body:\"\\u2022 Swipe: sets direction for armed ghosts.\\n\\u2022 Keyboard movement: WASD or Arrow keys.\\n\\u2022 Keyboard ghost controls: 1-4 selects a ghost, hold 1-4 to cycle that ghost's AI role.\\n\\u2022 Keyboard power-ups: F1-F8 uses the matching power-up slot in your HUD.\\n\\u2022 Backspace: leave run (with confirmation).\\n\\u2022 Tap-to-move: tap a walkable tile and your armed ghosts path toward that spot (enable in Settings \\u2192 Controls).\\n\\u2022 We recommend using a controller for the best experience, but swiping is still good.\\n\\u2022 Unarmed ghosts and Pellet Guy use passive AI movement.\\n\\u2022 Tap a ghost icon: arm/disarm that ghost.\\n\\u2022 Selected ghost can be directed instantly where legal.\\n\\u2022 Pausing and power-ups are available from the in-game HUD.\"},{title:\"PELLET GUY + POWER PELLETS\",body:\"\\u2022 Pellet Guy eats pellets as he moves.\\n\\u2022 Yellow power pellets make ghosts vulnerable for a short time.\\n\\u2022 Vulnerable ghosts can be eaten by Pellet Guy.\\n\\u2022 You can regain control through spacing, route cuts, and power-up timing.\"},{title:\"AI BEHAVIOR (QUICK GUIDE)\",body:\"\\u2022 Pellet Guy AI scales by level: early levels are mostly random, then it increasingly avoids nearby ghosts and takes safer routes.\\n\\u2022 At high levels, Pellet Guy has stronger awareness and becomes harder to predict/corner.\\n\\u2022 Unarmed ghosts use hunt AI: they usually chase Pellet Guy, with some randomness so routes are less scripted.\\n\\u2022 Ghost hunt aggression rises with level, so passive ghosts become better at pressure and cutoffs.\\n\\u2022 Magnet effects can temporarily alter these priorities.\\nGhost AI role options:\\n\\u2022 FREE: looser movement and less direct pressure.\\n\\u2022 HUNTER: direct chaser that prioritizes shortest pressure routes.\\n\\u2022 AMBUSHER: attempts to predict Pellet Guy movement and cut off escape routes.\\n\\u2022 PATROL: steadier lane control around spawn/nearby paths.\\n\\u2022 SOCIAL: prefers to stay within 5 tiles of another ghost.\\n\\u2022 CAUTIOUS: avoids danger zones and traps while still contesting space.\\n\\u2022 COWARD: keeps distance and drifts toward safer corners.\\n\\u2022 To switch AI roles, long press on the ghost you want to change.\"},{title:\"HAZARDS + TRAPS\",body:\"\\u2022 Pellet Guy can leave hazards (spikes/barricades) as stages progress.\\n\\u2022 Spikes kill ghosts on contact.\\n\\u2022 Barricades block routes temporarily.\\n\\u2022 Advanced teams can modify trap behavior (for example first-barricade skip or delayed spike arm).\"},{title:\"POWER-UPS + SHOP\",body:\"Power-ups are bought with Ghost Coins and can decide runs.\\nExamples: Speed Boost, Freeze, Magnet, Shield, Pellet Scatter.\\n\\u2022 Hardcore revive token only works in Hardcore conditions.\"},{title:\"STARS + LEVEL PROGRESSION\",body:\"Each level tracks stars and rewards cleaner clears.\\n\\u2022 Better pellet control and fewer mistakes = stronger star outcomes.\\n\\u2022 Gold stars and catches feed progression systems and unlock pacing.\"},{title:\"BONUS STAGES\",body:\"Every 5th level is a bonus game.\\n\\u2022 Rally Round, Cherry Chase, Time Attack, and Power Hunt can rotate.\\n\\u2022 Bonus stages are scored differently from standard catches.\\n\\u2022 Perfect bonus clears feed mission/stat progression.\"},{title:\"GAME MODES\",body:\"\\u2022 Classic: normal campaign progression.\\n\\u2022 Speedrun: fastest clears matter most.\\n\\u2022 Time Attack: fixed timer pressure.\\n\\u2022 Hardcore: no normal respawn safety.\\n\\u2022 Endless: roguelite scaling, blessing choices, and long-run economy.\"},{title:\"ENDLESS MODE DETAILS\",body:\"\\u2022 Milestone blessing pick every 5 levels.\\n\\u2022 Blessings include hunter scoring, Pellet Guy slow, ghost speed-up, second wind, rare continue discount, and super-rare 2-catch clears.\\n\\u2022 Continue cost scales per run; blessings can alter that cost.\\n\\u2022 Endless rewards long-term routing and coin management.\"},{title:\"TEAMS + PASSIVES\",body:\"Unlock teams through level/catch milestones.\\nPassives change strategy (examples):\\n\\u2022 Jackpot Crew: chance to double clear coins.\\n\\u2022 Golden Girls: chance for faster Pellet Guy respawn pacing.\\n\\u2022 Marathon Squad: small per-ghost-move chance to drop pellets on empty tiles.\"},{title:\"MISSIONS + LEADERBOARDS + STATS\",body:\"\\u2022 Daily missions grant extra Ghost Coins.\\n\\u2022 Leaderboards track major modes and lifetime totals.\\n\\u2022 Statistics gives run analytics (catches, clears, combos, bests, mode-specific records).\\n\\u2022 Hidden medals on run-end: \\ud83e\\udde8 Mine Sweeper (no spike triggers), \\ud83d\\udc7b Untouchable (0 ghost losses), \\u26a1 Speed Haunt (quick clear), \\ud83c\\udfaf Efficient Evil (catches without power-ups), \\ud83d\\udc80 Last Stand (win on final life).\"},{title:\"RUN IMPROVEMENT TIPS\",body:\"\\u2022 Spread ghosts to cut escape lanes, then converge.\\n\\u2022 Save key power-ups for unstable board states.\\n\\u2022 Respect hazard choke points before committing a route.\\n\\u2022 In Endless, pick blessings that match your run economy and risk profile.\"}];function h(){var n=(0,o.useRouter)();return(0,l.jsx)(t.SafeAreaView,{style:u.container,testID:\"tutorial-screen\",children:(0,l.jsxs)(s.ScrollView,{contentContainerStyle:u.content,showsVerticalScrollIndicator:!1,children:[(0,l.jsx)(s.TouchableOpacity,{style:u.backBtn,onPress:()=>n.back(),testID:\"tutorial-back-btn\",children:(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{style:u.backBtnText,children:\"\\u2190 BACK\"})}),(0,l.jsxs)(s.View,{style:u.headerCard,children:[(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{style:u.title,children:\"TUTORIAL\"}),(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{style:u.subtitle,children:\"Complete guide to modes, systems, and progression\"}),(0,l.jsx)(s.TouchableOpacity,{style:u.playableTutorialBtn,onPress:()=>n.push(\"/game?practice=1\"),testID:\"tutorial-hero-btn\",children:(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{style:u.playableTutorialBtnText,children:\"\\u25b6 PLA